Changelog: 13-11-2026 19:25:42

Version 0.2.1.

Changelog: 10-11-2026 00:39:40

Fixed. The global shortcut (Ctrl+Alt+F12) talks to the desktop portal through dbus-fast instead of dbus-next, which
is no longer maintained and does not load on Python 3.15 (it needs typing.no_type_check_decorator, which 3.15
removed): on Bazzite with Python 3.15 the shortcut failed and the shortcut service's test stopped ./test.sh. dbus-fast
is installed on Linux only, where the service runs, and the test skips on Windows.

Changelog: 04-11-2026 21:04:25

Version 0.2.0.

Changelog: 04-11-2026 20:08:16

Added. Nexus Demo Recorder runs on Windows (owner, 04-11-2026), where it records the Windows Portable Suite's
portal: a portal release (wp-portal-v<x.y.z>.zip) extracted in Downloads, or chosen, whose install.ps1 runs in a
PowerShell window of its own; the status it ends with goes back to the window as install.sh's does. There is no
install from the checkout on Windows. Ctrl+Alt+F12, which stops the recording, is a hot key of Windows' own
(RegisterHotKey, in a thread of its own) and says so when another program holds it. OBS is found in Program Files
and started from its own folder, as it needs to be, and the portal opened after the install is the installed
Windows-Portable-Suite.exe. The window's texts name PowerShell, Display Capture and Windows Portable Test there.
run.ps1 starts it, and run.sh from Git Bash takes .venv-windows. On Linux nothing changes; the tests run both
systems' paths on either system.

Changelog: 04-11-2026 19:05:17

Fixed. Two tests pass on Windows: the player's file is compared as a path, and the test manifest writes its paths
with forward slashes (a backslash in a TOML string is an escape).

Changelog: 02-11-2026 00:44:49

Added. Nexus Demo Recorder, a Nexus app in dev/demo/ (owner, 02-11-2026: the tools for working on the suites are
Nexus's, in one place, and the Media Tool, released as an app of the BC250 Bazzite Suite, was dev work in a
portal): the OBS part of the Media Tool (mtool-v1.0.1, its last release) as an app of its own. It records a demo of
a portal installation with OBS: an extracted portal release in Downloads, found by itself, or, without one, the
BC250 Bazzite Suite in this checkout; the optional app to show; the global shortcut of the desktop portal that
stops the recording and brings the window back; Recent recordings with the player. It runs from the checkout with
the dev venv (run.sh, bc250_core from core/), takes Nexus's design and icon (core's nexus.py), and is never
released (.checkout-only). The recordings go to ~/Videos/demos (they went to ~/MediaToolRecordings, which stays).
install.sh writes the launcher, menu entry and Desktop icon for this checkout, and removes the Media Tool's own
copy, venv and entries (and Simple Demo Tool's before it). The video tours and the icons went to Nexus Dashboard.
